   "source": [
    "# CSE476 Agentic AI & Intelligent Automation — Task 2 (CA2)\n",
    "## Project Q12: Automated Grant & Scholarship Application Evaluator\n",
    "\n",
    "**Architecture:** Multi-Agent Fan-Out / Fan-In with Microsoft Semantic Kernel, Grounded Rubric RAG, Shared State Store, and Append-Only JSONL Audit Logging.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Agent Roster:\n",
    "1. **Intake Agent:** Ingests raw dossier, validates Pydantic schemas, and initializes state.\n",
    "2. **Eligibility Verification Agent:** Checks hard minimum percentage ($\ge 60\%$) and income ceiling ($\le \\text{₹}600,000$). Disqualifies outright or flags missing data as `NEEDS_REVIEW`.\n",
    "3. **Merit Agent:** Evaluates academic percentage against a 40-point linear scaling formula.\n",
    "4. **Financial Need Agent:** Maps household income into progressive need scoring brackets (35, 28, 20, 10, 0).\n",
    "5. **Achievement Agent:** Evaluates co-curricular achievements, filters unverified entries, deduplicates titles/certificates, and caps at 25 points.\n",
    "6. **Panel Manager Agent:** Fans in specialist results, synthesizes composite score out of 100, assigns recommendation tier, and enforces exclusion of ineligible candidates.\n",
    "7. **Fairness Auditor Agent:** Audits score rationales against prohibited demographic attributes and verifies mathematical summation consistency."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import asyncio\n",
    "import json\n",
    "from decimal import Decimal\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from core import ensure_sk_compatibility\n",
    "from core.shared_state import StateStore\n",
    "from core.audit_logger import AuditLogger\n",
    "from core.scoring_config import RUBRIC_VERSION, get_configuration_hash\n",
    "from rag.retriever import RubricRetriever\n",
    "from orchestration.coordinator import ScholarshipCoordinator\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply Semantic Kernel forward-reference patch\n",
    "ensure_sk_compatibility()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"[INIT] System Initialized.\")\n",
    "print(f\"[RUBRIC] Version: {RUBRIC_VERSION} | Config Hash: {get_configuration_hash()[:16]}...\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1. Initialize System Components and RAG Retriever"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "retriever = RubricRetriever(\"rag/scholarship_rubric.md\")\n",
    "print(f\"Indexed {len(retriever.clauses)} rubric clauses successfully.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test Grounded RAG Query\n",
    "query = \"minimum academic percentage threshold\"\n",
    "matches = retriever.retrieve_relevant_clauses(query, top_k=2)\n",
    "for c in matches:\n",
    "    print(f\"-> Cited {c.clause_id}: {c.title}\\n   {c.text}\\n\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2. End-to-End Evaluation of a Single Applicant Dossier"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "store = StateStore()\n",
    "logger = AuditLogger(\"execution_audit.jsonl\")\n",
    "coordinator = ScholarshipCoordinator(store=store, logger=logger, retriever=retriever)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load sample candidate (Aarav Sharma)\n",
    "with open(\"data/applicants.json\", \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "    applicants = json.load(f)\n",
    "\n",
    "sample_candidate = applicants[0]\n",
    "print(f\"Evaluating Candidate: {sample_candidate['full_name']} (ID: {sample_candidate['applicant_id']})\")\n",
    "\n",
    "state = await coordinator.evaluate_applicant(sample_candidate)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n--- EVALUATION SUMMARY ---\")\n",
    "print(f\"Status: {state.status}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Recommendation: {state.recommendation}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total Score: {state.total_score}/100.0\")\n",
    "print(f\"  - Academic Score: {state.academic_result.score}/40.0\")\n",
    "print(f\"  - Financial Need Score: {state.financial_result.score}/35.0 (Band: {state.financial_result.income_band})\")\n",
    "print(f\"  - Achievement Score: {state.achievement_result.score}/25.0 (Verified: {state.achievement_result.verified_count})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Fairness Audit Passed: {state.audit_result.passed}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3. Multi-Agent Inter-Agent Execution Trace Stream"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Chronological Inter-Agent Communication Trace:\")\n",
    "for i, evt in enumerate(state.trace_events, 1):\n",
    "    print(f\"{i:02d}. [{evt.sender} -> {evt.receiver}] ({evt.event_type})\")\n",
    "    print(f\"    {evt.payload_summary}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4. Batch Pipeline Execution Over 17 Fictional Applicants"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(f\"Starting concurrent batch evaluation of {len(applicants)} candidate dossiers...\")\n",
    "all_states = await coordinator.evaluate_batch(applicants)\n",
    "print(f\"Completed batch evaluation of {len(all_states)} applicants.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "leaderboard = await coordinator.get_ranked_leaderboard()"
   ]
  },
